```

One note on the approach: the existing test `aTileCountsAsActiveWhateverItsSpacesOrCase` asserts that `activeMedicationNameKeys` returns name-only keys and that the name-only `isAlreadyActive` matches, and its assertions cannot be touched. So the route-aware check ships as a parallel pair (`activeMedicationKeys` / `isAlreadyActiveOnRoute`, keyed via `medicationNameRouteKey`) and the picker switches to it, while the name-only pair stays for the existing test and any name-level use. All existing assertions and the `medicationNameKey` behavior for the Recent filter stay as they are.
